content.text:
Fails in 48ms — so the waitFor loop sees only CONNECTING even after the full completion, meaning operation.progress stayed CONNECTING through the entire run... but the debug script showed SESSION_CREATED. Difference between test and debug: test's workshop passes `budgets: { guideTimeoutMs: 90_000, makerTimeoutMs: 90_000 }` and engine etc. Hmm what else... test `approvedProject` only for makerReady=false here.

OH. I see it: in the test file, `waitFor(() => ... progress?.phase)` — connectedOp = awaitedOp(sent).operation — the queue's op object. `operationOf(state, connectedOp.id)` — fine.

48ms — the whole test fails fast: meaning `waitFor` didn't expend its 4s budget; instead the assertion checked after `connected === null`?? waitFor returns first truthy value — progress?.phase string "CONNECTING" truthy → returns immediately at t≈10ms (before coordinator's async start finished!). The waitFor returns CONNECTING immediately (first poll at ~10ms), so assertion fails — it never waits for the phase to advance. Test bug! Fix: waitFor should wait for the phase to BE something: predicate returns progress only if it's SESSION_CREATED or WAITING_FOR_MODEL... i.e.:

```ts
const connected = await waitFor(async () => {
  const state = (await run.store.load()).state;
  const phase = operationOf(state, connectedOp.id).progress?.phase;
  return phase === "SESSION_CREATED" || phase === "WAITING_FOR_MODEL" || phase === "RECEIVING_OUTPUT" ? phase : null;
});
```

Also test 2: "expected 'AWAITING_RECONCILIATION'" but progress was...? Failed at waiting ABANDONED — got FAILED? Wait, guides.markFailed now uses classifyNativeError with unknown=true for NativeTimeoutError → ABANDONED. But test 2 failed with "expected: AWAITING_RECONCILIATION" — probably progress phase missing; markFailed finish sets `operation.result` etc, sets progress = null for failed/ABANDONED? guides.finish sets operation.progress=null unconditionally! Late reconcile marker must remain. For ABANDONED in guides.finish, keep progress as AWAITING_RECONCILIATION. Fix: in finish, ABANDONED → phase AWAITING_RECONCILIATION; else null.

Also test 9: exit → same ABANDONED with nativeSessionId — timed out waiting for ABANDONED — because speak error "Connection reset before the reply." — classifyNativeError: message matches ECONN? "Connection reset" — my regex `ECONN` doesn't match "Connection"... The failureIsUncertain regex `/timed out|timeout|ECONN|fetch|network|socket|unavailable|interrupted/i` — "Connection reset" contains none ("socket"? no). But classifyNativeError's last chain: /timed out|timeout|ECONN|fetch|network|socket|unavailable/ — "Connection reset before the reply."—contains "connect"? their regex in runs service had /\bECONN\b.../ hmm original had regex `ECONN` too... In service.classifyNativeError the timeouts regex matched ECONN... "Connection" doesn't match ECONN. So Classification → NATIVE_FAILED, unknown false → FAILED — but test 9 expects ABANDONED. Actually with speak throwing mid-call after session creation... uncertain because the message contains... let me set `uncertain` in guides.markFailed to also check Boolean(sessionId) when nativeSessionId was recorded (session existed → outcome unknown, salvage-able). rules: unknown || failureIsUncertain || (error carrying nativeSessionId && providerFailure null?) — maker's rule: failureIsUncertain(message, error) where nativeSessionId presence returns true. failures.failureIsUncertain checks error.nativeSessionId typeof string → true. My guides.markFailed should use `failureIsUncertain(message, error)` — error has nativeSessionId "ses_lost" → true → ABANDONED. In my edit, uncertain = classification.unknown || failureIsUncertain(message, error) → good: handles Connection-reset? failureIsUncertain(message...) checks error.nativeSessionId → string → true. So ABANDONED should happen... but test2/9 timed out waiting ABANDONED...

Test 9 timed out because the observed FAILED never became ABANDONED — right, uncertain false in old run (updates partially applied?). Test 2 failed with "expected AWAITING_RECONCILIATION" — it passed the ABANDONED wait but progress was null (finish clears). Both explained by finish progress clearing. Fix guides.finish: keep AWAITING_RECONCILIATION for ABANDONED.

