Flaky: "Expected revision 5, found 6" — after waitForOperation("SUCCEEDED"), a late progress write from the observing loop may still bump the revision (e.g., a phase write racing with the just-applied finish). The observe loop stops when finished — but a write already in flight (RECEIVING_OUTPUT with executeLatest) can land after the finish. My markProgress guard checks CURRENT status (terminal) and avoids mutation — but that still... wait if the guard returns the project unchanged, executeLatest still RECORDS THE ACTION and bumps revision! markProgress returns refreshNextAction(next) unchanged → save still bumps revision +1 with an action record. That causes the revision drift the test hits.

Fix in the source (better than test): writeProgress should skip recording when the operation is already terminal. Implement: in `writeProgress`, first load current state; if op terminal or not found → return without writing. There's an inherent race (load-then-write) but it makes the window tiny; the guard inside the mutation must ALSO avoid recording the action when nothing changed... executeLatest records the action unconditionally on a successful mutation. To be exact: make writeProgress:

```ts
export async function writeProgress(workflow, operationId, phase, detail) {
  const project = await workflow.get();
  const op = project.operations.find(o => o.id === operationId);
  if (!op || TERMINAL.has(op.status)) return;
  if (op.progress && op.progress.phase === phase && ...) skip? Also skip if phase already recorded at same or later rank: 
  if (op.progress && phaseRank(op.progress.phase) > phaseRank(phase)) return;
  if (op.progress?.phase === phase) return;  // already recorded
  await workflow.executeLatest(...);
}
```
This dedupes and prevents terminal mutations. Race between get and save remains but narrow.

Also update markProgress guard to leave progress unchanged if same phase exists (idempotent but the action record is what bumps revision...). With the pre-check in writeProgress, redundant writes mostly disappear.

Note progress.ts currently imports markProgress with a hardcoded terminal guard. Add terminall pre-check + same-phase skip in writeProgress.

Also the phase-guard: `const released = this.options.guide...` — implement now.

