Still fails in the full-suite context. Chain again: coordinator's `finish` (ABANDONED) → progress null (marker lost if recovery hadn't marked yet, fine) → then recovery marks marker. So the assertion undefined means the recovery didn't mark. Scenario: recoverAfterRestart's retried attempt... Let's trace the test: runMaker started; perform returns outcome "running" (not timedOut, stillRunning) → coordinator finish ABANDONED at ~rev N. Test waits for RUNNING then calls recoverAfterRestart. If coordinator's finish landed BEFORE recovery → recovery sees ABANDONED — not in QUEUED/RUNNING/WAITING list → `recovered = 0` → returns NULL without marking! The progress marker was cleared by finish (status ABANDONED progress null) → assertion undefined OR recovered null cases. My assumption that recovery only sees in-flight statuses fails when the coordinator's ABANDONED finish landed between waitFor and recovery.

Fix in source: `markRecovered`'s ABANDONED earlier too... Which piece sets the marker on coordinator ABANDONED? runs.finish now sets marker only if it existed before. If finish creates ABANDONED without marker, recovery must add one. Change recoverAfterRestart's predicate to include ABANDONED? No — recovered should not RE-mark ops already marked (idempotence + repeated recovery returns null). Predicate: statuses [QUEUED, RUNNING, WAITING_PERMISSION, COMPLETED_UNAPPLIED, ABANDONED] where progress?.phase !== "AWAITING_RECONCILIATION";

Terminate the finish → recovery marks; recovery→finish preserves. Either order converges to marker present. Adjust recoverOperation.

input.newString:
for (const operation of next.operations) {
  const needsRecoveryMarker = ["QUEUED", "RUNNING", "WAITING_PERMISSION"].includes(operation.status)
    || (["COMPLETED_UNAPPLIED", "ABANDONED"].includes(operation.status)
      && operation.progress?.phase !== "AWAITING_RECONCILIATION");
  if (needsRecoveryMarker) {
    operation.status = "ABANDONED";
    operation.statusReason = "application-restarted";
    operation.lastObservedAt = this.now().toISOString();
    operation.result = "The application restarted while this native operation was in flight. It was not repeated; reconcile the native session or mark it abandoned.";
    operation.progress = {
      phase: "AWAITING_RECONCILIATION",
      detail: "The native session can be reconciled after the restart; a late result is applied exactly once.",
      updatedAt: this.now().toISOString(),
    };
    recovered += 1;
  }
}

